    "summary": "Turn 27 fixed the applied-state proposition as its own obligation, exactly what the previous review's scope challenge required.\n\nWhy a new claim. The review of the applied-state artifact (05dc6a36…, executed as 2f186bc1…) was revision_needed on scope: the accepted claim C1-recovery-adopts-committed-vector explicitly excludes execution, so confirming applied-state convergence there would have treated an independent limit as a confirmation gate. The proposition is therefore fixed separately.\n\nNew obligation and check. Claim C3-applied-effect-follows-committed-vector (consensus safety, priority 3): when several replicas each hold the same instance committed and each applies it, the effect they apply for the instance's key must be the same, because the applied effect is determined by that instance's committed command vector. Its scope now includes applying the instance through the executor and excludes the production loop, watermarks, timing, client-visible replies and the history that produced each record; its grounding derives the duty from the executor and state application (strongconnect applies the component's commands and marks them EXECUTED; state.Command.Execute turns them into store effects), with an alternative reading recorded. A binding locates Exec.executeCommand, and the check reuses the harness that drives the confirmed recovery path, applies each replica's committed record with the real executor and compares the effects for the instance's key, with the committed_reply prerequisite as admission alias and instance identity correlation. The local construction run gives peer 04 against (void) at the recoverer and the third replica, i.e. applied_match false, so the formal outcome is left to the trusted runner and a fresh correspondence review.\n\nFraming detail. The question declares its core relationship through B11-prepare-resolution, whose attributed cross-activity effect is that the recovered value re-enters the normal accept and commit path (A1); B8-scc-closure, B7-execute-scheduler and B6-commit-install are named as support, and the fact is F2-committed-decision. The harness caller duties and its substitutions are recorded in the plan's semantic changes and uncertainties (direct execution, prepared committed record, no production loop).\n\nState. Audit spec version 6; the two confirmed claims and their reviewed checks are untouched; the accept-status candidate remains paused; the applied-state proposition now lives where it can be confirmed on its own terms, and no earlier result, premise or observation was weakened."
